-7e5e-585d-a9f1-baf4b638e989" :question/math-academy-id "q-75595" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,$ ${R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1},\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75595/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75595"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75508/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "ba3b7038-9810-596d-873a-58edbdfff711" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75508/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "973ffdfd-968b-59c9-8699-529f363de9f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75508/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "f2e44a19-aa80-514c-b6d6-c9108f9e37cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75508/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "aa809462-8786-5077-aaeb-dbd17df6e4a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75508/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "4927c9f3-d4cc-55b0-af43-b8c0d90bcfaa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75508/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "881a44d8-94d0-582e-91bc-336126c5a6aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75508/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer-field/choices ["q-75508/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" "q-75508/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" "q-75508/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-75508/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" "q-75508/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75508" :question/id #uuid "2eb6d032-088d-565d-ab8d-72bcf173e9b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-75508" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75508/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75508"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131347/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "e1e5bd9f-669b-5474-80ef-344d221820e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131347/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e9