\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75599/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75599"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131381/selection/7d20df1b7d193ad01fc3c52d3a802b29063e354540a0697a3feb2b12afddbbec" :answer/id #uuid "61a942d0-3f57-51be-934b-23a1d6f6f857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131381/selection/50316d2c254de6d451a6de8d2d579d6371d7903049f83f3d387a4cdffe668b6f" :answer/id #uuid "f220a910-1c8f-5ff5-9795-f881b26cc0fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131381/selection/faf0032b5437ce2e65fcf4b355a997ee8ed49c9935217023e334591d2a46dabe" :answer/id #uuid "367cdc21-d31c-5c70-99dd-6a04769ac3bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131381/selection/6db4cd32a4c08e598cbeb5990c5c34323416a4ecec6aa1e5d4e7dab1ccc5a892" :answer/id #uuid "2620eb0b-038f-5a5b-bc41-af20438232ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131381/selection/0057c496ff9cba3d54c6ca4eefa95e53d7262d22d63a62c56f10b3d629da4b37" :answer/id #uuid "c1434626-7592-55e2-8c20-d8e0763453d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131381/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd019b54-0c3a-52c1-961b-b6d468db5ece" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131381/selection/7d20df1b7d193ad01fc3c52d3a802b29063e354540a0697a3feb2b12afddbbec" :answer-field/choices ["q-131381/selection/7d20df1b7d193ad01fc3c52d3a802b29063e354540a0697a3feb2b12afddbbec" "q-131381/selection/50316d2c254de6d451a6de8d2d579d6371d7903049f83f3d387a4cdffe668b6f" "q-131381/selection/faf0032b5437ce2e65fcf4b355a997ee8ed49c9935217023e334591d2a46dabe" "q-131381/selection/6db4cd32a4c08e598cbeb5990c5c34323416a4ecec6aa1e5d4e7dab1ccc5a892" "q-131381/selection/0057c496ff9cba3d54c6ca4eefa95e53d7262d22d63a62c56f10b3d629da4b37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131381" :question/id #uuid "a618d522-1f89-5278-907e-8cb0fd49bf99" :question/math-academy-id "q-131381" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131381/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a4b135f-df0d-5443-bb93-796f32c380c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31871/selection/94d22e263354b49612ed782e9b6c9a57925a285e4faabbab9703671aa8afaf72" :answer/id #uuid "ba5e7730-2ce7-5404-a715-71e79b625181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31871/selection/c2c698c6d4cb7f833cef4eca1f75b5ee2d48a8ef81a9048f0f92b8a8e66db8a8" :answer/id #uuid "47ad9c3b-7721-57b0-9963-ebd1e32af9c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31871/selection/4183799149ce44fad0fb3288330d42eb331ca0680e66a32cdba54e56d0fe4cc9" :answer/id #uuid "58574ec8-399a-5f6e-b6f2-d2f9038956ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31871/selection/cf17f893cca766b458eb4f28e252ebdf04942b507b10642f1ac22f58bcfb56f5" :answer/id #uuid "da5b93c8-c6e6-57ab-8524-d917ba5b90fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{B}^{-1}=[\