a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42988"] :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42988/selection/ma-v1/780e0e7958df6c6edb416b9eef4e603aa25d61b8210ebe034f80a742eb1b48c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-131999/selection/38733643a7782b36b9a9ebeec0a0aa14aa3145bae68928ef575be22f921dc5f3" :answer/id #uuid "a0add77f-f4a9-52b8-ac7e-0782ca701f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131999/selection/73a8951f7eb0c167105724e15ab41c62d364ab86e1832cc8f26336c232696a6d" :answer/id #uuid "dc0d2e25-3329-595f-9c6d-1a1ae7bac970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131999/selection/a5e638b4161a6c831673fe378b7ae2beb921e5495c22abd6a9bb60ca07b908c5" :answer/id #uuid "7b6b33e8-f12d-54e7-b2d7-7ec6d92a3bea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131999/selection/add1e024b9e87cfd79cd986e95f22ace73e5ead79047fd6fac2528844c026988" :answer/id #uuid "99a9f4d6-6be9-586f-9d55-3ac54729adfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131999/selection/77a2fef4c5482b22c0163f5f3517be0940e0c08ddb84bd9e195c05b055513100" :answer/id #uuid "905d066b-e2ca-5190-b661-5873cd339c41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131999/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d397cac0-ceb4-58dc-9e71-50229d91b300" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131999/selection/77a2fef4c5482b22c0163f5f3517be0940e0c08ddb84bd9e195c05b055513100" :answer-field/choices ["q-131999/selection/38733643a7782b36b9a9ebeec0a0aa14aa3145bae68928ef575be22f921dc5f3" "q-131999/selection/73a8951f7eb0c167105724e15ab41c62d364ab86e1832cc8f26336c232696a6d" "q-131999/selection/a5e638b4161a6c831673fe378b7ae2beb921e5495c22abd6a9bb60ca07b908c5" "q-131999/selection/add1e024b9e87cfd79cd986e95f22ace73e5ead79047fd6fac2528844c026988" "q-131999/selection/77a2fef4c5482b22c0163f5f3517be0940e0c08ddb84bd9e195c05b055513100"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131999" :question/id #uuid "41dc19c4-f697-52b3-b9b5-76ded5157f14" :question/math-academy-id "q-131999" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $Y$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Y\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $Y$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $Y$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Y\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${Y}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{Y}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131999/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31946/selection/633ddebfb06e0c55ee7e94ff04397b0ac4476f1ccad475dc31fda97363b9ba42" :answer/id #uuid "60ac1883-2e34-5c35-97a1-ba1e506e83b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31946/selection/245b51e1b9134e07deb7982838c140fd44033f1707f72ea61dd50a1db5058839" :answer/id #uuid "7c456437-90b5-5e39-ba4d-ae5ddfa501c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31946/selection/acda2184e9107dfb5984d7d06f0a9d21402149428218b7f3ac214fedfe8b06b2" :answer/id #uuid "8a2da5c8-1943-5ad8-ac16-45c37c0ef121" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31946/selection/3b20cbb975d6c5959bae32d1059ae15b9a84fd4ab1c94c4050d85fc58e6f641b" :answer/id #uuid "234be48b-228b-517f-803a-c07955b146f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31946/selection/1a6b3507622e701ff71c9e93dacc506d2d6b2b94797540ad0642b43630a7eca9" :answer/id #uuid "0eab3c25-cc50-5c7d-bc59-a051c74256cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31946/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da349521-b51d-51e7-bf38-f7dd7a3726d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-31946/selection/3b20cbb975d6c5959bae32d1059ae15b9a84fd4ab1c94c4050d85fc58e6f641b" :answer-field/choices ["q-31946/selection/633ddebfb06e0c55ee7e94ff04397b0ac4476f1ccad475dc31fda97363b9ba42" "q-31946/selection/245b51e1b9134e07deb7982838c140fd44033f1707f72ea61dd50a1db5058839" "q-31946/selection/acda2184e9107dfb5984d7d06f0a9d21402149428218b7f3ac214fedfe8b06b2" "q-31946/selection/3b20cbb975d6c5959bae32d1059ae15b9a84fd4ab1c94c4050d85fc58e6f641b" "q-31946/selection/1a6b3507622e701ff71c9e93dacc506d2d6b2b94797540ad0642b43630a7eca9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-31946" :question/id #uuid "76bc14dd-df85-52d6-bc25-d8ef7d523eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-31946" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $U$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[U\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $U$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $U$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[U\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${U}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{U}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-31946/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-31946"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131386/selection/0d75d58f6defd6e961cdfc7d005976afa35cf2b1bbb5b5623fc7632e57941ea1" :answer/id #uuid "46172b88-eceb-5e1c-bccc-e0b842cf34fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131386/selection/8265d61838e978a7ecad1e167804f50d574a00f378ee7a9ed921bb331797b3ae" :answer/id #uuid "2765f195-a12d-5343-a730-a276085f4ed3