nding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 10 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+10{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 10 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+10{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131386/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131386"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43004/selection/1a414695ea365fe9750ae233c36a3a1dde6bec30e602bd98ac3d572c1b82300f" :answer/id #uuid "5272bedb-f5cb-5248-a6e2-8c4780c44589" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43004/selection/7b155d3815c0a305397c44cc0faa521f2b9073b8f5f67909beb2382265a292e8" :answer/id #uuid "466f40a1-7d60-58